
This project analyzes a used car sales dataset sourced from Kaggle to uncover patterns in vehicle sales, pricing, resale value, performance, fuel efficiency, and manufacturer performance.

The analysis was designed from a business and decision-making perspective, with the goal of identifying the factors associated with stronger sales performance and understanding how different manufacturers, models, and vehicle types compare across key business metrics.

The project uses Python, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, and Seaborn for data preparation, exploratory data analysis, KPI development, statistical analysis, and visualization.

🎯 Business Objectives
The analysis focuses on answering questions such as:

Which manufacturers generate the highest total sales?
Which vehicle models are the best sellers?
How do vehicle types compare in terms of sales, pricing, resale value, and efficiency?
Do higher-priced vehicles necessarily achieve lower sales volumes?
What is the relationship between horsepower and sales?
Does fuel efficiency have an observable relationship with sales?
Which vehicles provide the strongest horsepower relative to their price?
Which models demonstrate strong 4-year resale value retention?
What numerical variables show the strongest relationship with sales?
