📊 KPI Development
A KPI table was created to provide a high-level overview of the dataset and establish the core business metrics.

Key KPIs include:

Total Models
Total Manufacturers
Total Sales
Average Vehicle Price
Average 4-Year Resale Value
Average Horsepower
Average Fuel Efficiency
Average Resale Retention
These KPIs provide a concise snapshot of the overall vehicle market represented in the dataset.

🏭 Manufacturer Performance Analysis
Manufacturer-level analysis was performed using grouped aggregations to compare:

Number of models
Total sales
Average price
Average resale value
Average horsepower
Average fuel efficiency
The analysis also identifies the top manufacturers by total sales and visualizes their performance using bar charts.

This helps evaluate manufacturer-level market performance and identify leading players within the dataset.

🚘 Best-Selling Models
The project identifies the highest-selling vehicle models based on total sales volume.

The analysis compares top-performing models across:

Sales volume
Manufacturer
Price
4-year resale value
This provides a model-level view of which vehicles have achieved the strongest market demand.

💰 Pricing vs. Sales Analysis
One of the key business questions explored is:

Do expensive vehicles actually sell less?

A scatter plot and correlation analysis were used to examine the relationship between vehicle price and sales volume.

This analysis helps assess whether pricing appears to be associated with sales performance and provides a foundation for further statistical or predictive modeling.

♻️ Resale Value & Retention Analysis
A resale retention metric was derived to evaluate how vehicle value is retained relative to its original sales/price measure.

The analysis identifies models with stronger resale retention and compares vehicles based on:

Original price
4-year resale value
Resale retention percentage
This provides an additional perspective on vehicle value beyond initial sales performance.

🚙 Vehicle Type Analysis
Vehicles were grouped by type to compare:

Number of models
Total sales
Average price
Average resale value
Average horsepower
Average fuel efficiency
This allows comparison of market performance across different vehicle categories and helps identify which vehicle types have stronger overall sales performance.

🔥 Performance vs. Price
To evaluate value for money, a custom metric was created:

Horsepower per $1,000

This metric compares vehicle performance against price and identifies vehicles that provide relatively high horsepower for their cost.

The analysis ranks the top-performing models using this derived metric while also considering their sales performance.

